{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773077062,"nonce":"hsvbpMJEiyGtFJn7XMRWcaipew8=","title":"Auto-save race: edit arriving during in-flight PUT leaves isDirty falsely false","message":"In App.tsx auto-save useEffect: the debounce timer fires, starts updateGraph(), and calls markSaved() on completion. If a new edit arrives while updateGraph() is in-flight, isDirty becomes true again momentarily — but markSaved() then clears it unconditionally, leaving the store believing the edit is saved when it is not.\n\nNo new timer will start because isDirty was briefly true but the useEffect dependency did not change (isDirty was already true before the in-flight save ran).\n\nFix: add an in-flight ref (savingRef) or capture a \"last-dirty-at\" timestamp before the request, and skip markSaved() if new edits arrived during the request.","files":null}]}